("Which is a primary source of liquidity for a company?",
 "Cash and short-term investments", ["Renegotiating its debt contracts", "Filing for bankruptcy protection", "Liquidating plant assets"],
 "Primary sources are cash on hand, short-term funds, cash flow from operations and bank lines. Renegotiating debt and liquidating assets are secondary sources that signal weaker finances."),
("A company with a high level of fixed financing costs has high financial leverage. As a result, its net income is:",
 "More sensitive to EBIT", ["Less sensitive to EBIT", "Independent of sales", "Always higher than EBIT"],
 "Interest is a fixed charge, so a given change in operating income produces a larger percentage change in net income. That raises both expected ROE and its volatility."),
